  "notes": "Entirely business-type entity (community college): governmental fields null. Only the College columns are used; the Foundation (component unit) columns are excluded. Receipts/disbursements from the Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p3-4); no single printed totals for receipts or disbursements, so computed. Interest on indebtedness (printed negative within nonoperating revenues) recorded as a debt service interest disbursement. Capital appropriations 16,671,213 and gain on disposal 141,782 (printed under Other revenues, below income before other revenues) recorded in business_type.other_financing, not receipts. Spending is listed by object only, so function 'instruction' was chosen with review; depreciation put in 'other' with review. The Statement of Cash Flows continues on a page not in the trimmed PDF (net change and beginning/end cash not shown); proprietary beginning/ending cash null. Detail: General Fund revenues and expenditures on the budgetary basis (not GASB; equipment expensed, tuition not net of scholarship allowances): revenue lines p6 including the '(Add) to/use cash reserves' balancing line (-3,124,822) recorded as other financing printed inside the revenue total; expenditures by program and object p7, with grand total 111,900,098 on p8 (by-object grand totals on p8 tie to the sums). SBITA assets/liabilities classed under other assets/debt. Noncurrent compensated absences and sick leave in other liabilities. Read pages 1-8 of 8.",
